Reviewed the full diff against master. Cause confirmed in Datadog: owners log copied=false then ready=false 3 s after the last confirmed copy, every ~5 s, on all four pairs. Consumers of a serving NAT's Ready: none act on it while it serves (controller checks report.Ready only without a lease, and PeerReady of the standby for handovers; the updater checks the standby's PeerReady). So the change only affects the reported flag and the former owner's first rounds after a handover, where its window shrinks back at the next round. A stale peer report still clears PeerReady. New test fails without the fix and passes with it. go vet and go test ./... pass.
